{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"code":"store.items","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates the observer class tree and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"text":") are unnecessary. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already checks equality on ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Effect-Threading","text":"Effect Threading","level":2},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"title":"Effect","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxObservable","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"kind":"article","title":"Design Principles","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"title":"Plugin Architecture"}}}